#
# A logic:ActionableFrontier citing a witness that witnesses NOTHING: no settled
# predicate, no consumed budget. It is strictly worse than the frontier that cites
# no witness at all, because this one satisfies every law that merely COUNTS the
# citation — the presence law passes, the not-budget-exhausted test passes
# vacuously (there is no evaluation status to be exhausted), and an operator reads
# a certified-closed roster.
#
# A witness with no content records nothing that could be false, and evidence that
# cannot be wrong is not evidence.
#
# MUST trip logic:FrontierClosureRequiresSaturationConstraint.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

ex:frontierEmptyWitness a logic:ActionableFrontier ;
    rdfs:label "a frontier citing a witness that certifies nothing"@en ;
    logic:frontierSaturationWitness ex:emptySaturation .

ex:emptySaturation a logic:SaturationWitness ;
    rdfs:label "a saturation witness carrying neither settled predicates nor a budget"@en .
